-- Every fact the new rows rest on stands on two hosts in
-- scripts/data/<sport>ConnectionsVerified-2026-10.json.
--
-- The guard: a row is rewritten only while it still holds one of the boards
-- known from before this round (jsonb equality, so key order and spacing do not
-- matter): the file's board, and for bconn-009, 012 and 015 also the seed's
-- own spelling (migration 20260526000007 wrote their labels with a dash the
-- file has since lost). A row that holds anything else is left alone and named
-- in a NOTICE, never overwritten blind. The live tables hold more rows than the
-- files (299 baseball, 20 NFL, 20 NHL at the last count); rows past the files
-- are not touched here, and the lead's export run of
-- US_CONN_LIVE=baseball=<file>,nfl=<file>,nhl=<file> node scripts/simUsConnectionsFacts.mjs
-- is the first look at them.
--
-- A saved daily guess keeps the groups it solved as they were saved (the sport
-- hooks), so on the day a rewritten board is dealt, a guess saved before the
-- apply keeps showing the OLD group, false member and all, counts it toward
-- 4/4 and strands the new members as tiles (played on a runner by the round's
-- review). Apply on a day this rewrites no dealt board:
-- node scripts/qa/connectionsDealtDay1558.mjs <sport>=<export.json>,... <YYYY-MM-DD>
--
-- A re-run after a good apply is a no-op (no row still holds an old board).

